WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.360
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.989
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.289 --> 00:00:16.923
Unit sixteen: Giving Presentations. Today you will plan and deliver a short academic presentation.

4
00:00:17.223 --> 00:00:19.922
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.867 --> 00:00:24.111
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.137
Presentation.

7
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.730
Presentation means a talk to an audience.

8
00:00:30.317 --> 00:00:31.991
Give a short presentation.

9
00:00:32.583 --> 00:00:35.387
Your turn. Say: Presentation.

10
00:00:38.233 --> 00:00:39.432
Presentation.

11
00:00:40.183 --> 00:00:41.150
Audience.

12
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:44.324
Audience means the people who listen.

13
00:00:44.917 --> 00:00:46.243
Look at the audience.

14
00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.653
Your turn. Say: Audience.

15
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.455
Audience.

16
00:00:54.217 --> 00:00:55.125
Slide.

17
00:00:56.117 --> 00:00:58.128
Slide means one page of a talk.

18
00:00:58.717 --> 00:01:00.403
Keep each slide simple.

19
00:01:01.017 --> 00:01:03.506
Your turn. Say: Slide.

20
00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:07.403
Slide.

21
00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.302
Eye contact.

22
00:01:10.317 --> 00:01:12.514
Eye contact means looking at listeners.

23
00:01:13.117 --> 00:01:14.408
Make eye contact.

24
00:01:15.017 --> 00:01:17.750
Your turn. Say: Eye contact.

25
00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:21.706
Eye contact.

26
00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:23.312
Pace.

27
00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:26.444
Pace means speed of speaking.

28
00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:28.446
Control your pace.

29
00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:31.354
Your turn. Say: Pace.

30
00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:34.946
Pace.

31
00:01:35.683 --> 00:01:36.766
Rehearse.

32
00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.889
Rehearse means to practise before.

33
00:01:40.483 --> 00:01:41.844
Rehearse the talk.

34
00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.485
Your turn. Say: Rehearse.

35
00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:49.404
Rehearse.

36
00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:51.000
Visual.

37
00:01:52.017 --> 00:01:54.074
Visual means a picture or chart.

38
00:01:54.683 --> 00:01:56.230
Use a clear visual.

39
00:01:56.817 --> 00:01:59.190
Your turn. Say: Visual.

40
00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:02.930
Visual.

41
00:02:03.683 --> 00:02:04.684
Handout.

42
00:02:05.683 --> 00:02:08.345
Handout means a paper given to listeners.

43
00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:10.148
Give a handout.

44
00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.275
Your turn. Say: Handout.

45
00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:17.076
Handout.

46
00:02:17.867 --> 00:02:21.425
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.283 --> 00:02:24.585
Visal, how do I start a presentation?

48
00:02:25.683 --> 00:02:35.592
Greet the audience, say your topic and give an outline, for example Today I will talk about three points. This helps listeners follow.

49
00:02:36.683 --> 00:02:38.288
How should my slides look?

50
00:02:39.383 --> 00:02:47.736
Keep each slide simple with a short heading, a few key words and one clear visual. Do not read the slides word for word.

51
00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:50.292
What about nerves?

52
00:02:51.383 --> 00:03:01.977
Rehearse several times, speak slowly and make eye contact. Pause between points and end with a short summary and an invitation for questions.

53
00:03:03.133 --> 00:03:04.808
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:09.240
Grammar focus: Future forms for outlining a talk.

55
00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:10.785
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:11.483 --> 00:03:13.494
I will begin with the main causes.

57
00:03:14.383 --> 00:03:16.453
I am going to show three charts.

58
00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:24.612
Outline a talk with I will, I am going to or I would like to, followed by a base verb: I will begin with the causes.

59
00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:29.036
Be careful! Don't say: I will to begin with causes.

60
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.557
Say: I will begin with causes.

61
00:03:33.857 --> 00:03:35.020
No to after will.

62
00:03:35.833 --> 00:03:38.579
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:40.693
A Short Talk.

64
00:03:40.993 --> 00:03:44.142
Nary gives a five-minute presentation on recycling.

65
00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:47.713
She greets the audience and gives a clear outline.

66
00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.477
Her slides have short headings and one visual each.

67
00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:55.012
She speaks slowly and makes eye contact.

68
00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.766
At the end she summarises and invites questions.

69
00:03:59.867 --> 00:04:03.810
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.684
An audience is the people who blank.

71
00:04:06.984 --> 00:04:10.081
A, drive. B, listen. C, sell.

72
00:04:13.633 --> 00:04:15.621
The answer is B: listen.

73
00:04:16.783 --> 00:04:19.154
Eye contact means looking at the blank.

74
00:04:19.454 --> 00:04:22.597
A, floor. B, clock. C, listeners.

75
00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:28.272
The answer is C: listeners.

76
00:04:29.417 --> 00:04:31.289
To rehearse is to blank before.

77
00:04:31.589 --> 00:04:35.172
A, practise. B, sleep. C, eat.

78
00:04:38.733 --> 00:04:40.861
The answer is A: practise.

79
00:04:42.017 --> 00:04:43.436
Slides should be blank.

80
00:04:43.736 --> 00:04:47.227
A, blank. B, simple. C, crowded.

81
00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:52.894
The answer is B: simple.

82
00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:55.597
How long was Nary's talk?

83
00:04:55.897 --> 00:05:00.270
A, one hour. B, one second. C, five minutes.

84
00:05:03.833 --> 00:05:05.937
The answer is C: five minutes.

85
00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:10.471
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:11.317 --> 00:05:13.189
How do you give a good presentation?

87
00:05:21.983 --> 00:05:23.449
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:23.749 --> 00:05:36.446
I greet the audience and give a clear outline. My slides are simple with one visual each. I rehearse, speak slowly, make eye contact and end with a summary.

89
00:05:36.746 --> 00:05:38.386
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:39.283 --> 00:05:44.269
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and future forms for outlining a talk.

91
00:05:44.569 --> 00:05:48.777
Today's value is confidence. Speak up and be proud of who you are.

92
00:05:49.077 --> 00:05:51.985
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:54.914
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

